e diagnosis and outcome of colorectal cancer: a prospective study</article-title><source>Eur J Surg Oncol</source><year>1999</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>178</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Surg Oncol||25|173||bib18|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10218461</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rupassara</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ponnusamy</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Withanage</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Milewski</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A paradox explained? Patients with delayed diagnosis of symptomatic colorectal cancer have good prognosis</article-title><source>Colorectal Dis</source><year>2006</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>429</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Colorectal Dis||8|423||bib19|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16684087</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stubbs</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Symptom duration and pathologic staging of colorectal cancer</article-title><source>Eur J Surg Oncol</source><year>1986</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>130</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Surg Oncol||12|127||bib20|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3709816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>WONCA</collab></person-group><article-title/><source>ICPC-2. International Classification of Primary Care. Prepared by the Classification Committee of WONCA</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Oxford: Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wra